  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 143 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nA sfc cold front to our north will slowly sink south today and \ntonight. We could see some isolated to scattered showers/storms pop \nup with the heat of the day ahead of the front. Right now location \nis lower confidence as there are no boundaries around to focus \ndevelopment. Timing still looks to be now through 06Z at the latest \ntonight. Some of these storms could be strong to severe for damaging \nwinds. Conditions are dry the rest of the weekend behind the cold \nfront. Temperatures are slightly cooler with the exception of the \nfour western SEMO counties plus Stoddard, New Madrid, and Fulton \ncounties where a Heat Advisory is in effect for tomorrow for one \nmore day of 100+ degree heat indices. \n\nThe slightly cooler and drier weather continues through Monday \nbefore the ridging aloft to the west re-centers overhead by Tuesday \nmorning. Heat indices return to the upper 90s on Tuesday and back to \nthe 100+ degree mark on Wednesday. The ridge begins to flatten and \nbreak down Wednesday afternoon into Thursday. Slightly cooler and \nmore unsettled weather for Thursday ahead of an approaching cold \nfront. 20-30% PoPs move through the area on Thursday just ahead of \nthe front. Scattered 15-20% PoPs are in the forecast on Friday \nbehind the front. Overall the forecast is lower confidence \nheading into next weekend due to model differences.",
